  TypeScript, JSON, plugin, MCPB, and docs checks. The full host baseline is 719/719.
  CI on `main` green
  (bundle/test/validate-mcpb/validate-plugin, `test` job ~9min).
- Plugin: `himalaya` installed and enabled via marketplace (Data-Wise/himalaya-mcp)
- Homebrew: data-wise/tap/himalaya-mcp — confirmed at v2.1.0 (`url`/`sha256`
  verified live against the tap repo, PR #208 merged).
- Aggregator marketplace: Data-Wise/claude-plugins `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` confirmed
  `himalaya` @ 2.1.0 (auto-synced by aggregator-sync.yml, PR #45 merged).
- Docs: deployed at https://Data-Wise.github.io/himalaya-mcp/ (Deploy Docs workflow green on
  the v2.1.0 merge commit).
- Bundle: ~910KB (esbuild), .mcpb: ~253KB
- opencode: `himalaya` MCP server configured in `~/.config/opencode/config.json` (enabled,
  entry `/opt/homebrew/opt/himalaya-mcp/libexec/dist/index.js`, `HIMALAYA_ACCOUNT=unm`).
- Worktrees: only the main checkout remains, clean on `dev`. Removed 2026-08-16 during backlog
  triage — `feature/docs-plugin-fixes` and detached `gracious-wilson-4b3f6a` worktrees, plus the
  `feature/docs-plugin-fixes` (`395a18a`) and `feature/docs-680-tests-v2` (`8b2ba1b`) branches
  local and remote. Both were docs-only and fully superseded: their unique prose (standalone +
  plugin bundle wording, stale-plugin-directory doctor fix, 15s probe note, `email`→`himalaya`
  plugin rename) and all three CHANGELOG entries already landed on `dev` via `0ef207f`, and their
  test counts (680/691) were stale against 719.
- Maintenance follow-up: Issue #121 — **root-caused 2026-08-16, and the failing job turns out to
  be redundant.** `homebrew-release.yml`'s `upload-mcpb` job has failed on all five releases
  (v2.0.2–v2.1.0), but no release was ever missing its asset: for v2.1.0 the
  `himalaya-mcp-v2.1.0.mcpb` asset was created at `17:35:08Z`, one second *before* the release was
  published (`17:35:09Z`) and ~9.5 min before the failing job ran (`17:44:42Z`). No workflow does
  `gh release create`, so the asset is attached by the local release pipeline at release-creation
  time; the CI job only ever tried to re-upload a file the release already had.
  Mechanics of the failure: the `validate` job's `Upload MCPB artifact` step matched nothing
  (`##[warning]No files were found with the provided path: himalaya-mcp-v*.mcpb`) and, lacking
  `if-no-files-found: error`, stayed green — so the error surfaced one job later as a misleading
  "Artifact not found for name: mcpb-bundle". **Why the glob missed is still unconfirmed and is
  CI-specific**: a working-directory mismatch is ruled out (`checkout@v7`, no `path:`, no
  `defaults.run.working-directory`), `scripts/build-mcpb.sh:51-59` hard-exits when the file is
  absent, and a local `npm run build:mcpb` puts `himalaya-mcp-v2.1.0.mcpb` (253 KB) at the repo
  root exactly where the glob expects. See "Next Action" for the fix.

## Install

```bash
# Homebrew (recommended)
brew tap data-wise/tap
brew install himalaya-mcp

# Claude Code plugin (from GitHub)
claude plugin marketplace add Data-Wise/himalaya-mcp
claude plugin install himalaya

# Claude Desktop (.mcpb extension)
# Download .mcpb from GitHub Releases, double-click to install
himalaya-mcp install-ext

# Claude Desktop (legacy CLI setup)
himalaya-mcp setup

# Diagnose installation
himalaya-mcp doctor
himalaya-mcp doctor --fix
```

