  defense in depth. PR #123 merged to `dev`, verified 669/669 tests green in Docker.
- 2026-08-04: Released v2.0.3 (PR #124 → `main`, merge commit `0283f0a`) — version bump
  committed directly to `dev` (`c6ae7f3`), Docker-verified (37/37 files, 669/669 tests, exit 0)
  before push. CI green on both the `dev` push and the PR (bundle/test/validate-mcpb/
  validate-plugin). Tagged `v2.0.3`, built `.mcpb` locally, `gh release create` with the asset
  attached directly. Homebrew formula and aggregator marketplace both independently verified
  live at v2.0.3 (not assumed). Issue #121's `.mcpb` CI artifact-upload flake recurred again
  (empty 22-byte artifact download) — harmless here since the release already had the real
  asset from the manual upload; formula update job itself succeeded regardless. `dev` fast-
  forward-merged to match `main` (0 commits behind either way).

## Next Action

- No active release work — v2.1.0 is fully shipped and verified end-to-end.
- **Fix next:** issue #121 (`.mcpb` release artifact upload) — NOT a flake, and **not
  load-bearing**. The `upload-mcpb` job has failed on all five releases (v2.0.2–v2.1.0) while
  every release still shipped its `.mcpb`, because the local release pipeline attaches the asset
  at release-creation time and the CI job only re-uploads it (see the timing evidence below).
  Decision needed: **delete the redundant `upload-mcpb` job** and its feeding
  `Upload MCPB artifact` step (simplest — five releases prove the job is dead weight), **or**
  keep it as a CI-side safety net and make it honest by adding `if-no-files-found: error` plus a
  pre-upload `ls -la` diagnostic so the next failure names its own cause. Either way, the silent
  `if-no-files-found` default is the defect that hid this for five releases.
- **Pending:** PR #82 (HTML compose_email, base=main) — the previously recorded manifest blocker
  is GONE (a 2026-08-07 force-push reduced the `mcpb/manifest.json` diff to +1/−1, a single tool
  description; it does not delete 8 tools + 1 prompt). Branch merges clean. Real blockers now:
  (1) `skills/compose/SKILL.md` promises multipart/alternative with a text/plain part, but the
  code sends HTML-only by design; (2) `html: false` is ignored — no opt-out from auto-detection;
  (3) `isHtmlContent()` false-positives on plain prose (`a\s`, `p\b`, `link\b`, `meta\b`);
  (4) HTML + attachments untested. Also needs retargeting `main` → `dev`.
- **Pending:** PR #115 (coerce numeric IDs to string in Zod schemas, base=main) — valid and still
  needed; all 13 `z.string()` id sites remain unpatched on `dev`, merges clean. Needs retargeting
  `main` → `dev`.
- **Pending:** PR #117 (Dependabot "dev-deps group") — this is the TypeScript 6→7 **major** bump
  (`^6.0.3` → `^7.0.2`) relabeled; it supersedes the previously-deferred PR #97, which is now
  closed. `test` job is red. Hold for the same deliberate review, or split the `@types/node`
  26.1.1→26.2.0 patch out from the major.
- Otherwise: all features complete, project in maintenance mode. Possible future directions:
  - Bundled .mcpb variant with universal himalaya binary (~19 MB)
  - Code signing + notarization (Apple Developer, $99/yr)
  - Official Anthropic extension directory listing
  - Obsidian adapter — export emails to vault as markdown notes
  - Templates — reusable email templates for common replies

